00:35.260 --> 00:38.720
Paris. The end of the 19th century.
Beneath the glass ceiling of the Galerie du Roy,
one can see the thin silhouette of a Japanese girl named Yune.
For now, only a few Parisians know of her arrival...

00:35.260 --> 00:38.720
The crossing in a foreign maze

00:38.720 --> 00:44.100
As I open the gate and step out into the street

00:44.730 --> 00:48.770
asa no hikari ga mabushii

00:44.730 --> 00:48.770
朝の光が眩しい

00:44.730 --> 00:48.770
I can see the sun shining brightly

00:51.780 --> 00:56.780
doko kara ka nagareru hanauta ni

00:51.780 --> 00:56.780
どこからか流れる鼻歌に

00:51.780 --> 00:56.780
I can hear humming in the distance

00:57.950 --> 01:01.700
kokoro hazumi tokete yukuyo

00:57.950 --> 01:01.700
心弾み解けてゆくよ

00:57.950 --> 01:01.700
It moves me and melts my heart

01:04.910 --> 01:10.380
mabuta tojireba ukabu egao

01:04.910 --> 01:10.380
目蓋閉じれば浮かぶ笑顔

01:04.910 --> 01:10.380
I can see that smile when I close my eyes

01:11.550 --> 01:16.970
omoidasu tabi ni namida hitotsu

01:11.550 --> 01:16.970
想い出すたびに涙ひとつ

01:11.550 --> 01:16.970
It brings me to tears whenever I remember it

01:17.470 --> 01:20.600
te wo hiroge hashiridase

01:17.470 --> 01:20.600
手を広げ　走りだせ

01:17.470 --> 01:20.600
Spread your arms out and take off

01:20.600 --> 01:23.930
hi no ataru toori wo

01:20.600 --> 01:23.930
陽のあたる通りを

01:20.600 --> 01:23.930
Down the streets where the lights shine

01:23.930 --> 01:30.480
michiyuku hito ni genki ni aisatsu

01:23.930 --> 01:30.480
道行く人に元気にあいさつ

01:23.930 --> 01:30.480
Cheerfully greet people walking down the city streets

01:30.480 --> 01:37.110
atarashii kimochi de shinkokyuu shitara

01:30.480 --> 01:37.110
新しい 気持ちで　深呼吸したら

01:30.480 --> 01:37.110
Take a deep breath to refresh yourself

01:37.110 --> 01:45.620
kono sekai wa hora itsudemo kimi no mono

01:37.110 --> 01:45.620
この世界はほら、いつでも　君のもの

01:37.110 --> 01:45.620
And this world will always be yours

01:51.000 --> 02:01.010
Episode 09 :

01:51.000 --> 02:01.010
" Secret "

02:03.850 --> 02:07.350
<i>Yune-chan is just like me when I was younger.</i>

02:07.350 --> 02:09.940
<i>Yune is nothing like you.</i>

02:09.940 --> 02:11.400
<i>She's become a rumor, you know?</i>

02:12.110 --> 02:16.780
<i>She's always at your side, looking up to you.</i>

02:16.780 --> 02:20.360
<i>I only came because you did us a favor.</i>

02:20.360 --> 02:22.740
<i>I really didn't want to bring her over.</i>

02:22.740 --> 02:24.990
<i>Yune's being manipulated by Alice,</i>

02:24.990 --> 02:26.500
<i>just like a doll.</i>

02:27.000 --> 02:30.420
<i>Is that something you should be saying?</i>

02:32.080 --> 02:35.250
<i>I like that part of you...</i>

02:35.250 --> 02:36.960
<i>but that's a bit cruel.</i>

02:37.340 --> 02:40.970
<i>No matter how much thought you put into a dress or decorations,</i>

02:40.970 --> 02:43.930
<i>he won't notice it.</i>

02:43.930 --> 02:46.850
<i>Even if he does, it would just be-</i>

02:48.310 --> 02:49.640
<i>What's so funny?</i>

02:50.980 --> 02:53.520
<i>No, um...</i>

02:53.520 --> 02:54.820
<i>I...</i>

02:55.570 --> 02:57.490
<i>I feel the same way!</i>

03:01.610 --> 03:07.410
<i>I was happy that I could talk so much about Claude-sama.</i>

03:08.500 --> 03:10.000
<i>Try it on.</i>

03:12.540 --> 03:14.170
<i>I'll help you. </i>

03:21.800 --> 03:24.680
I'm back, Yune-chan!

03:27.430 --> 03:30.350
How adorable!

03:30.350 --> 03:32.980
This is my most memorable dress!

03:32.980 --> 03:35.900
Yes, Camille-sama told me about it.

03:35.900 --> 03:36.730
Really?

03:36.730 --> 03:38.530
Let me see the entire thing!

03:39.820 --> 03:42.200
You're actually wearing my dress!

03:42.200 --> 03:43.070
It's a dream come true!

03:43.070 --> 03:44.820
I'm so happy!

03:46.660 --> 03:48.370
Where's Camille?

03:48.370 --> 03:50.500
She was here until just a moment ago,

03:50.500 --> 03:52.710
but she had to prepare to go out.

03:53.370 --> 03:54.580
I see.

03:54.580 --> 03:57.420
She must have to tighten her corset again...

03:58.710 --> 04:05.050
Noblewomen are required to wear a corset in order to marry a nobleman.

04:06.800 --> 04:09.970
I could never bear such a thing,

04:09.970 --> 04:12.810
but my sister never complains.

04:13.440 --> 04:18.940
She must be planning to marry the son of a very noble family, just as Mother and Father expect her to.

04:21.190 --> 04:22.530
Oh, right!

04:22.530 --> 04:25.610
I came here to get you because everything has been prepared!

04:25.610 --> 04:27.450
Let's go!

04:27.450 --> 04:28.910
O-Okay!

04:28.910 --> 04:29.950
Come on! Hurry up!

04:30.410 --> 04:31.750
Alice-sama!

04:33.750 --> 04:36.000
Um, Alice-sama...

04:36.540 --> 04:37.960
Not yet.

04:38.210 --> 04:40.550
You'll be so surprised!

04:41.130 --> 04:42.010
Now.

04:42.800 --> 04:43.880
How is it?

04:49.560 --> 04:50.680
Do you like it?

04:50.680 --> 04:51.720
Yes!

04:51.720 --> 04:54.730
I remembered that I had some Japanese tea!

04:54.730 --> 04:58.360
I just <i>had</i> to serve you some!

04:59.400 --> 05:03.490
I learned how to make tea the way Japanese people do.

05:22.420 --> 05:23.420
Well?

05:23.420 --> 05:24.510
Right...

05:24.920 --> 05:25.880
Help yourself!

05:25.880 --> 05:26.800
O-Okay!

05:38.980 --> 05:41.070
Thank you very much for this tea.

05:41.070 --> 05:43.570
That's how you say it?!

05:58.670 --> 06:02.550
Japanese people don't put sugar or cream in tea.

06:03.420 --> 06:04.670
They don't?!

06:04.670 --> 06:06.340
I'll make another one!

06:06.340 --> 06:09.760
It's fine, you already made a bowl,

06:09.760 --> 06:12.560
so I'll gladly take this.

06:24.360 --> 06:25.820
It's good.

06:30.820 --> 06:32.320
I'm supposed to drink this, right?

06:33.700 --> 06:36.330
It might be too bitter for-

06:38.620 --> 06:40.210
Are you all right?

06:40.210 --> 06:41.210
I'm fine!

06:41.210 --> 06:44.170
I want to have it the same way Japanese people do!

06:48.840 --> 06:49.880
My leg!

06:50.380 --> 06:51.430
Milady!

06:51.430 --> 06:53.640
Are you all right?!

06:53.640 --> 06:56.020
What has happened to your foot?

06:56.020 --> 06:57.220
Alice-sama!

07:08.530 --> 07:11.030
I love you, Claude.

07:12.110 --> 07:13.450
Camille?

07:13.450 --> 07:16.330
I really do love you.

07:16.700 --> 07:21.250
So even if we grow up and I get married,

07:21.250 --> 07:23.130
will you still come over to play?

07:23.790 --> 07:26.800
Mother dislikes stray cats.

07:26.800 --> 07:33.970
It reminds her of a prostitute or <i>amant</i> when they
randomly barge into the house as if they belong there.

07:34.350 --> 07:36.220
Poor cat...

07:37.810 --> 07:40.140
I like stray cats more!

07:42.350 --> 07:46.860
Does that mean I'm the same as a stray cat?

07:46.860 --> 07:49.110
Yes. It's fine, right?

07:50.110 --> 07:52.570
You should be proud of yourself.

07:59.620 --> 08:00.580
Come in.

08:00.580 --> 08:03.120
She is waiting for you.

08:05.170 --> 08:06.500
Claude!

08:06.500 --> 08:07.630
Look!

08:10.340 --> 08:11.470
What's that?

08:12.930 --> 08:15.010
It's the newest bicycle!

08:15.010 --> 08:17.010
Wow! What's this?

08:17.300 --> 08:20.890
The wheels are both the same size!

08:20.890 --> 08:22.730
Try it out!

08:23.770 --> 08:25.190
Give it a ride.

08:25.600 --> 08:26.480
All right!

08:42.790 --> 08:44.790
You should try this too, Camille!

08:45.210 --> 08:47.000
I'm fine!

08:49.590 --> 08:50.420
Claude!

08:56.470 --> 08:58.350
Look, an automobile!

08:58.350 --> 08:59.100
Automobile?

08:59.430 --> 09:03.100
Automobiles will replace horse carriages from now on as a sign of status.

09:03.430 --> 09:06.020
It says they run using an engine and gasoline.

09:06.940 --> 09:08.650
It must be expensive.

09:08.650 --> 09:10.400
Father's going to buy one soon.

09:10.820 --> 09:11.780
Seriously?

09:11.780 --> 09:14.110
The Blanche family leads such a different lifestyle.

09:14.110 --> 09:18.570
You could probably go on forever with this.

09:19.950 --> 09:23.080
Railroads are still in development.

09:23.080 --> 09:27.370
It will be much easier to go on vacations using them!

09:27.920 --> 09:30.960
You can even go on a trip to the beach!

09:30.960 --> 09:32.380
A trip?

09:33.840 --> 09:36.840
Common people don't have that kind of time to spare.

09:38.680 --> 09:40.010
Fine.

09:41.260 --> 09:42.930
What are you so cranky about?

09:43.390 --> 09:44.930
I won't give you any more.

09:47.850 --> 09:48.690
Why not?

09:48.690 --> 09:49.520
You're so stingy!<i></i>

09:49.520 --> 09:51.730
It's a rare confection.

09:51.730 --> 09:53.570
I had to order it specially.<i></i>

09:55.320 --> 09:56.400
No fair!<i></i>

09:56.610 --> 09:58.450
Give me some, too!<i></i>

09:58.450 --> 09:59.530
No!<i></i>

09:59.530 --> 10:00.530
Yes!<i></i>

10:04.910 --> 10:06.120
Delicious!<i></i>

10:09.750 --> 10:10.540
It's sweet!<i></i>

10:11.920 --> 10:12.630
Here.<i></i>

10:19.510 --> 10:20.840
A steam engine!<i></i>

10:23.220 --> 10:24.680
Camille!<i></i>

10:25.720 --> 10:27.230
Let's go to the station together!<i></i>

10:28.020 --> 10:29.480
Why so suddenly?<i></i>

10:29.480 --> 10:30.900
Let's go see the steam engine!<i></i>

10:30.900 --> 10:33.230
I saw a timetable on a poster in the city!<i></i>

10:33.230 --> 10:35.860
We should be able to see it if we go now!<i></i>

10:39.150 --> 10:40.070
I'm not going.<i></i>

10:40.450 --> 10:41.740
I'm not interested.<i></i>

10:42.450 --> 10:45.290
You seemed so excited when you talked about them before.<i></i>

10:45.950 --> 10:47.160
It'll be awesome!<i></i>

10:47.160 --> 10:50.870
It looks way bigger than a horse carriage once you get close!<i></i>

10:50.870 --> 10:53.170
You can go alone.<i></i>

10:53.170 --> 10:54.380
What?<i></i>

10:54.380 --> 10:55.880
Fine.<i></i>

10:55.880 --> 10:58.470
Oh, look at this book!<i></i>

10:59.170 --> 11:03.470
It's a story about a person who went around the world in eighty days.<i></i>

11:04.140 --> 11:08.930
He went from England to Egypt, India, Japan, and America,<i></i>

11:08.930 --> 11:12.310
using only boats and trains!<i></i>

11:26.030 --> 11:28.700
You've gotta pay to watch, kid.<i></i>

11:28.700 --> 11:30.460
Hand me the money.<i></i>

11:30.870 --> 11:33.250
I just have to pay, right?<i></i>

11:38.840 --> 11:39.800
Yes!<i></i>

11:43.180 --> 11:44.600
Camille!<i></i>

11:45.680 --> 11:47.010
Claude!<i></i>

11:47.930 --> 11:50.310
Don't shout so loudly.<i></i>

11:50.310 --> 11:52.980
There's a puppet show at <i>L'Avenue des Champs-Élysées.</i>

11:52.980 --> 11:54.560
Let's go watch it together.<i></i>

11:54.560 --> 11:55.730
A puppet show?<i></i>

11:55.730 --> 11:57.690
I've got enough money!<i></i>

11:57.690 --> 11:58.650
See?<i></i>

11:59.320 --> 12:00.740
I have enough for you, too.<i></i>

12:03.320 --> 12:05.570
Puppet shows are too childish.<i></i>

12:06.530 --> 12:08.410
I'm not going.<i></i>

12:08.410 --> 12:10.200
I don't want to go outside.<i></i>

12:13.870 --> 12:14.750
I know!<i></i>

12:14.750 --> 12:16.420
Let's go to the <i>Galerie</i>, then!

12:16.420 --> 12:18.550
It's just like your backyard,<i></i>

12:18.550 --> 12:21.090
and there's an underground passage below the path,<i></i>

12:21.090 --> 12:23.800
connecting the entire <i>Galerie!</i>

12:23.800 --> 12:26.800
It's dark and scary, but it'll be fun!<i></i>

12:26.800 --> 12:29.930
Oh, and there's a weird guy named Alan,<i></i>

12:29.930 --> 12:31.890
who's the printer's son, by the way,<i></i>

12:31.890 --> 12:33.980
who says silly things all the time.<i></i>

12:33.980 --> 12:35.850
I'll introduce you to him!<i></i>

12:35.850 --> 12:38.520
I told you, I don't want to go.<i></i>

12:39.860 --> 12:41.530
Leave me alone.<i></i>

12:43.610 --> 12:45.030
Fine, whatever!

12:45.530 --> 12:49.200
Go have fun with all of the stuff in those books and pictures.<i></i>

12:54.710 --> 12:55.790
Here you go.<i></i>

12:56.210 --> 12:57.420
Thanks!<i></i>

12:58.130 --> 12:59.750
Juice, anyone?<i></i>

13:00.210 --> 13:01.510
Anyone?<i></i>

13:01.510 --> 13:03.220
Anyone?  <i></i>

13:03.220 --> 13:05.470
Hey, have you guys kissed?<i></i>

13:03.220 --> 13:05.470
Juice, anyone?<i></i>

13:06.090 --> 13:07.640
Who're you talking about?<i></i>

13:07.640 --> 13:09.430
You know, from the Blanche family.<i></i>

13:10.720 --> 13:12.060
Who cares?<i></i>

13:13.680 --> 13:14.810
Yeah,<i></i>

13:14.810 --> 13:20.980
the son of a metal craftsman in the <i>Galerie</i> would never be fitting for a wealthy family's daughter.

13:21.360 --> 13:25.320
Well, if you keep up the relationship and become an <i>amant,</i> then...

13:25.320 --> 13:28.450
Do you even know what that means, Alan?<i></i>

13:29.620 --> 13:31.990
O-Of course I do!<i></i>

13:31.990 --> 13:34.660
Hey, wanna go to the <i>Jardin des Plantes?</i> <i></i>

13:31.990 --> 13:34.660
Garden of plants.

13:34.660 --> 13:37.920
They've got a new bear named Martin-kun.<i></i>

13:37.920 --> 13:41.290
No, zoos are too childish.<i></i>

13:42.250 --> 13:43.130
What?<i></i>

13:44.340 --> 13:45.630
Shoot, it's raining!<i></i>

14:12.740 --> 14:14.450
Not yet.<i></i>

14:14.450 --> 14:17.330
The Mistress is still preparing.<i></i>

14:17.330 --> 14:18.710
I don't mind.<i></i>

14:18.960 --> 14:22.090
At least let her be free within the house.<i></i>

15:07.760 --> 15:10.050
And then, my husband-<i></i>

15:11.180 --> 15:12.050
Hm?<i></i>

15:16.430 --> 15:18.430
I want a picture book, Dad!<i></i>

15:18.430 --> 15:19.810
Which one?<i></i>

15:19.810 --> 15:22.690
I'm sure it would look excellent on you.

15:22.690 --> 15:25.400
What kinds of hats do you have?

15:25.400 --> 15:27.820
Binge drinking at this hour?

15:27.820 --> 15:29.360
It's like a replacement for water.

15:29.360 --> 15:31.280
Hey now,

15:31.280 --> 15:33.240
our wine is of the finest quality!

15:43.880 --> 15:46.590
The lamp decorations that I saw there were-

15:50.550 --> 15:55.260
Is there a metal sign store near here named <i>Enseignes du Roy</i>?

15:56.510 --> 16:00.270
<i>Enseignes du Roy</i> is just ahead, mademoiselle.

16:01.480 --> 16:02.730
Thank you.

16:30.050 --> 16:31.550
Take the next one, Claude.

16:31.550 --> 16:32.300
Okay!

17:02.450 --> 17:04.410
Where's the coal, Claude?!

17:04.410 --> 17:05.790
C-Coming!

17:06.250 --> 17:07.420
Camille...!

17:11.550 --> 17:12.550
Camille!

17:27.060 --> 17:30.570
I told you, didn't I? The <i>Galerie</i>'s connected underground.

17:31.980 --> 17:33.940
Quit slacking off, kid.

17:33.940 --> 17:36.030
Let me go!

17:48.960 --> 17:50.340
Claude!

17:50.340 --> 17:52.090
Why are you running away?

17:52.090 --> 17:53.130
Let go!

17:53.130 --> 17:56.880
You should've just come with me if you wanted to see the outside.

17:56.880 --> 17:58.260
What's up with you?

18:00.140 --> 18:05.020
My nannies are keeping you a secret under the condition that I'll never leave the house.

18:05.430 --> 18:07.390
If Mother finds out...

18:07.390 --> 18:10.770
You're just afraid of your parents finding out?

18:10.770 --> 18:12.650
You're such a coward.

18:12.650 --> 18:13.650
Yes.

18:14.570 --> 18:17.110
If it's my fault alone, I'll be punished.

18:17.610 --> 18:19.990
But if you're with me,

18:19.990 --> 18:24.540
you'll be punished, and we'll never be able to see each other again!

18:24.540 --> 18:28.290
I don't want to lose my right to meet with you!

18:41.180 --> 18:42.510
Milady,

18:44.260 --> 18:45.970
are you ready?

18:45.970 --> 18:46.850
Yes.

18:48.810 --> 18:51.400
Tighten it more.

18:51.400 --> 18:53.860
Please don't push yourself.

18:53.860 --> 18:55.860
I'm not.

19:15.590 --> 19:17.050
Please come again!

19:17.050 --> 19:18.510
Promise?

19:18.510 --> 19:20.800
Thank you for everything.

19:20.800 --> 19:22.800
Please thank Camille-sama, too.

19:22.800 --> 19:23.510
Understood.

19:23.510 --> 19:25.510
Well then, excuse me.

19:25.510 --> 19:27.930
Have a wonderful evening!

19:33.560 --> 19:37.730
Camille-sama is a very kind person.

19:38.940 --> 19:40.860
What makes you say that?

19:42.320 --> 19:44.740
You trust people too easily.

19:44.740 --> 19:49.250
She shared something precious to her.

19:58.300 --> 20:02.380
<i>This room holds many of my happiest memories.</i>

20:03.840 --> 20:07.850
This dress was part of Camille-sama herself.

20:08.680 --> 20:12.270
Camille-sama cares very deeply for her sister.

20:13.060 --> 20:20.320
I heard that a corset is necessary for a noblewoman to marry a nobleman.

20:27.990 --> 20:34.920
I think Camille-sama bears the weight of her corset not for herself, but rather...

20:37.710 --> 20:41.300
<i>I don't want to lose my right to meet with you!</i>

20:41.300 --> 20:45.340
<i>...and I get married, will you still come over to play?</i>

20:50.180 --> 20:52.180
You think that way as well?

20:53.310 --> 20:55.560
No, I...

20:57.560 --> 20:59.070
I don't know.

20:59.730 --> 21:00.860
Right.

21:07.030 --> 21:11.620
Then, I might be the one who needs to learn more.

21:40.940 --> 21:47.530
aa marude yume wo miteiru you na

21:40.940 --> 21:47.530
ああ　まるで夢を見ているような

21:40.940 --> 21:47.530
Ah, it's as if I'm in a dream

21:47.530 --> 21:53.330
yawarakana hikari no naka de

21:47.530 --> 21:53.330
やわらかな光の中で

21:47.530 --> 21:53.330
As I lie here in this tender light

21:53.330 --> 22:04.340
me wo tojite mimi wo sumasereba kikoete kuru

21:53.330 --> 22:04.340
目を閉じて　耳を澄ませれば　聞こえてくる

21:53.330 --> 22:04.340
When I close my eyes and listen, I can hear it

22:06.170 --> 22:19.230
atatakaku watashi wo yobu yasashii sono koe ga

22:06.170 --> 22:19.230
暖かく私を呼ぶ　優しいその声が

22:06.170 --> 22:19.230
That kind voice that warmly calls to me

22:21.810 --> 22:28.400
afureru omoi wo tsutaetai kono te kara

22:21.810 --> 22:28.400
溢れる想いを　伝えたいこの手から

22:21.810 --> 22:28.400
I want to extend my feelings with these hands

22:28.400 --> 22:34.700
kotoba ja nakute kokoro de tsunagaru

